'''''Paleoteius''''' is an [[extinct]] genus of [[lizard]] from the [[Late Cretaceous]] ([[Maastrichtian]] age) [[Allen Formation]] of Argentina. The genus contains a [[Monotypic taxon|single species]], '''''Paleoteius lakui''''', known from a partial skull and fragments of the postcranial skeleton. It has apparent affinities to the clade [[Scincomorpha]], and potentially the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Xantusiidae]], although its exact relationships differ based on the [[phylogenetic]] methodology used. ''Paleoteius'' is the most complete fossil terrestrial lizard known from the Late Cretaceous of South America.<ref name="Paleoteius" />

